Z||000000||saleenfiero||05-10-2001||12:48 AM||||I was talking to my buds at viperclub.org (yeah, like 50% of them really own vipes).  Anyways, one was talking about seeing clear spark plug wires that you can see the spark or something.  Sounds intriguing.  Any 411?<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||12
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||05-10-2001||06:59 AM||||My first thought is - impossible. You only see a spark when there's a gap and the current arcs across this gap, and wires that had that many gaps in them along the whole length would be useless.<P>Sounds like someone was pulling someone else's leg - along the lines of "horn fluid", "rotating the air in your tires", "muffler bearings", etc. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||05-10-2001||07:22 AM||||I think this may be a set with clear end caps with an LED in the plug cap. I,ve seen them advertised somewhere in a magazine.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||05-10-2001||08:44 AM||||I will post my insightful knowledge on this one. You can do it, with neon tubes. I've seen it done on TLC I think it was, on a motorcycle. The guy who does custom bikes in California(was at Daytona Bike Week too) has a motorcycle(his own) that is done like this. Looks most 'wicked' or 'groovy'<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||05-10-2001||10:08 AM||||Have you ever gone to a "Monster Truck" show?<P>"Monster Vette" which was at the Minot (ND State Fair) back in the early 90's had very cool (I think Neon) plug wires.  They lit up (flashed) when she was running!  Different color wires!  Friend of mine I believe has pictures of her.  I will see if I can get one and scan it.<P>Found some info:  <A HREF="http://dennistaft.freeservers.com/monvet.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://dennistaft.freeservers.com/monvet.htm</A>   Check out the <B>FEATURES:</B><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||05-10-2001||03:34 PM||||not sure about wires, but you can get special plugs for tuning a carb called "Colortunes".. they allow you to see the color of the flame inside the cylinders, to adjust the air/fuel ratio for the best performance. they won't stand up to driving though, just idling in the shop..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000006||Philphine||05-10-2001||04:38 PM||||i've seen the plug caps that light up advertised before, but not for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||05-10-2001||05:10 PM||||Years ago I've seen those on a Monster truck.  I heard they didn't hold up well with all that pounding the truck goes through, but for a show car, it would look pretty cool.  All that flashing coming out your vents and from under the car would confuse a lot of people that see it.:confuses:?..  Probably wouldn't go over well with the city police. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||05-10-2001||07:12 PM||||I know that you can get clear distributor caps.  They're a big deal in the VW circle because on sandrails and bajas the engine is in clear view, and it's cool at night.  Also they cost the same as a regular cap.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
